<title>HONG KONG: CIBC CEF sets call warrants on blue chip basket.</title>
<headline>CIBC CEF sets call warrants on blue chip basket.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Imperial Bank of Commerce, London Branch, said on Wednesday it launched 160 million American-style call warrants on a basket of blue chip stocks.</p>
<p>Each basket comprises of:</p>
<p> HSBC Holdings Plc			 0.02  shares</p>
<p> Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd    0.25  shares</p>
<p> Hutchison Whampoa Ltd		   0.075 shares</p>
<p> Sun Hung Kai Properties Ltd	   0.045 shares</p>
<p>Ten warrants control one basket.</p>
<p> STRIKE PRICE	 HK$17.2865    PREMIUM	 13.5 PCT</p>
<p> ISSUE PRICE	  HK$0.3366     GEARING	 5.41x</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	   25.JUN.98     MIN EXER LOT  10,000</p>
<p> REFERENCE SPOT     HK$18.1963</p>
<p> LISTING		HONG KONG</p>
<p> NOTE:    PHYSICAL OR CASH SETTLEMENT AT ISSUER'S DISCRETION</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
